<p>				NOTES</p>
<p>1. The Iranian year runs from March 21 to March 20. The first quarter ends on June 21, the second quarter ends on September 22, and the third quarter ends on December 21.</p>
<p>(In Iran's Islamic calendar, the year 1374 corresponds to 1995/96 in the Gregorian calendar, 1375 corresponds to 1996/97, 1376 corresponds to 1997/98, and so on.)</p>
<p>2. Includes $411 million of reschedulings under reconciliation. Actual and contingent total external obligations -- including opened letters of credit not yet consigned and future interest -- amounted to $31.1 billion at the end of the third quarter of 1996/97.</p>
<p>3. The official base rate applies to oil export receipts, imports of essential goods and services, debt service and imports related to large national projects.</p>
<p>4. The official export rate applies to non-oil export and service receipts, and imports and service payments applicable to the base rate.</p>
